            <title>[LU-20902] sanity test_413m/418: weighted round-robin MDT allocation leaves inode counts unbalanced</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20902</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Both test_413m and test_418 failed together in the sanity run of&lt;br/&gt;
test_group review-dne-zfs-part-1, session&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/4fbbc1db-4d3e-4135-a359-33083963b0bd" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/4fbbc1db-4d3e-4135-a359-33083963b0bd&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
on patchset 3 of change 69427 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17601" title="sanity: 413a Failed with 'subdirs shouldn't be evenly distributed: 21 - 19 &amp;lt;= 2' " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17601"&gt;LU-17601&lt;/a&gt; lmv: pick mkdir MDT by&lt;br/&gt;
weighted round-robin), the last of an unmerged stack (changes&lt;br/&gt;
69423-69427) reworking the MDT QoS weighted round-robin allocator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_413m: "MDT0 has 65 2nd stripes, want 70", outside the&lt;br/&gt;
+-MDSCOUNT tolerance the test allows for the weighted round-robin&lt;br/&gt;
placement of the second stripe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_418 in the same session: df -i reports 1245595 total inodes&lt;br/&gt;
while lfs df -i's per-target sum is 1286040; MDT0002's own total of&lt;br/&gt;
159289 is far below the other three MDTs' 356126-393147, so df and&lt;br/&gt;
lfs df disagree on the aggregate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Neither is new to patchset 3: the same two subtests fail with the&lt;br/&gt;
same signatures on the series' earlier changes 69423 ("MDT0 has 68&lt;br/&gt;
2nd stripes, want 59") and 69425 ("MDT0 has 66 2nd stripes, want&lt;br/&gt;
72"; df/lfs df inode mismatch), before 69427's own diff is even&lt;br/&gt;
applied, so this is not something 69427 introduces. The per-target&lt;br/&gt;
inode-count disagreement in test_418 looks tied to the dynamic&lt;br/&gt;
bytes-per-inode weight estimate 69425 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16678" title="LOD QOS object allocation improvement" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16678"&gt;LU-16678&lt;/a&gt;) added for QoS&lt;br/&gt;
weighting, which likely also feeds the per-MDT weight test_413m&lt;br/&gt;
checks; no existing ticket describes either failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69427-ps3-2250f0fafdb6 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69427" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69427&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
